  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe radial cross-drill hop between quarter-turn stations was sized by a closed form that assumes each mouth sits on its station's centre line. An off-centre pair - (8,-6) along -X and (-6,8) along -Y on an r10 bar - chorded 10.757 mm from the spindle, the r2 drill's rim 1.24 mm inside the bar, and #77's rapid proof refused the op (safe, but an ordinary pair of cross holes could not be drilled).\n\n- `traverse_s` (crates/motion/src/drilling/cross.rs) now takes the two holes. It keeps the closed form `hop_s * sqrt(2 / (1 + cos dtheta))` whenever that plane already clears - every on-centre pair, so existing chains and goldens do not move - and otherwise measures the chord between the two real hop points (new `chord_reach`, segment-to-spindle distance in XY), grows the plane until the closest approach reaches `hop_s`, then bisects back to the smallest clear plane. Opposite stations still take the end-face detour.\n- Decision recorded in `RECOMMENDED.md` (#81).\n\n## Readings\n\nThe pair now drills: no post-blocking warning, every rapid keeps the r2 rim outside the r10 bar. No golden file changed.\n\n## Gate (own worktree build, current main)\n\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --tests`: green except `swarf_pose_continuity` x2 (known pre-existing on main).\n- Every app binary touching cross/lathe/mill-turn drilling (drilling_cross*, lathe_*, stitch_cross, golden_cl, solid_law_goldens, ...): green except `drilling_axial::a_drill_where_the_model_has_no_hole_is_convicted` (known pre-existing on main).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Pinning test\n\n`drilling_cross_stock::a_station_change_with_mouths_off_their_centre_lines_hops_clear` - the (8,-6)/(-6,8) pair modelled in the bar (the #117 part law reads the model), lathe and mill-turn. On main it fails with the old refusal (\"cross-drill rapid 4 passes 10.757 mm from the spindle ...\"); on the branch it passes. It replaces the old `a_station_change_whose_chord_would_clip_the_bar_is_refused_by_name`, which pinned that refusal.\n\nChangelog: Cross-drill station changes with off-centre holes hop clear of the bar instead of being refused\n\nOutside contributor PR (fork).\n\nFixes #81\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
